# Threads Holo Ticket — a 300x400 event ticket with a holographic Skia sheen (driven by Y rotation and the device rotation sensor); tap flips it 180° with a spring, horizontal drags spin it freely and release into a clamped decay.
# What this test covers: tap-to-flip front→back (QR) and back, flipping again mid-spring, a slow drag through the
# 90° edge (front/back swap), fast flings both ways (withDecay clamped to ±1080), tapping to stop a decay mid-spin
# (cancelAnimation + snap to the nearest side), drags starting in the 50 pt hit slop outside the ticket, a vertical
# drag (no rotation), and a rapid tap burst.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/threads-holo-ticket"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait "text" "TUE 14 JAN" 10000
wait 800
# Flip to the back, and back to the front.
press 201 437
wait 900
press 201 437
wait 900
# Flip and flip again mid-spring.
press 201 437
wait 200
press 201 437
wait 1000
# Slow drag past the 90° edge.
gesture pan 120 437 160 0 900
wait 600
gesture pan 280 437 -160 0 900
wait 600
# Fast flings both ways; tap to catch the decay mid-spin.
gesture pan 100 500 250 0 120
wait 400
press 201 437
wait 1000
gesture pan 330 500 -280 0 120
wait 1800
gesture pan 100 500 260 0 100
wait 300
press 201 437
wait 1200
# Drags starting in the hit slop just outside the ticket.
gesture pan 201 210 120 0 500
wait 600
gesture pan 370 560 -150 0 500
wait 600
# Vertical drag on the ticket: no horizontal translation.
gesture pan 250 380 0 120 500
wait 800
# Rapid tap burst.
press 201 437 --count 5 --interval-ms 120
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
